1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,100
Take a square wave.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,000
One sine comes close.

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,340
Add odd sines, each one smaller.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,600
Sine 3x: a third as tall.

5
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:14,670
5x, 7x, and the corners sharpen.

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,130
It squares up, except at the jump.

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,100
More terms only make the overshoot

8
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:21,800
thinner.

9
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,400
About nine percent of the jump.
